// Test: bugfixes/typed_emission_stmt_call_bridge_registered_1edabe431cad
// Grammar: external block declaration + functions block (grammar.ebnf §external_block, §functions_block)
// Regression: dashboard fp 1edabe431cad.
//   Reported error code: TYPED-EMISSION-DUAL-SHIP-BLOCKED.
//   A plugin that dual-shipped v1 and v3 expansion paths and declared
//   `_stmt_call` in its `external:` block failed to load with
//   "unknown import: env::_stmt_call". The typed-emission bridge for
//   `_stmt_call` was not registered on the wasmtime linker even though
//   plugins compiled against Amendment 3 (compiler 0.30.408+) started
//   emitting imports for it.
//
//   Fix: `_stmt_call` bridge landed at
//   src/plugins/typed_emission/bridges.rs:661-665 as part of Amendment 3
//   in compiler 0.30.408. The bridge accepts (ctx, callee_lp, args_json_lp)
//   and returns a statement handle.
//
//   Anchor: this repro is the sanitized minimal from the dashboard entry.
//   It declares `_stmt_call` in an `external:` block and defines the two
//   dual-ship entry points (`expand_block_typed` for v3, `expand` for v1).
//   Under compiler 0.33.3+ this compiles cleanly — the presence of the
//   bridge registration means the emitted WASM import can be satisfied
//   at plugin load time.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.30.408
// Expected output:
// stmt-call-bridge-ok

external:
	integer _stmt_call(integer ctx, string callee, string args_json)

start:
	print("stmt-call-bridge-ok")

functions:
	integer expand_block_typed(integer ctx, string b, string a, string body)
		return 0
	string expand(string b, string a, string body)
		return body
